[h1]Battlezone 98 Redux: Unofficial Community Patch & Campaign Rewrite[/h1]
[i]An open-source native community patch and campaign overhaul for Battlezone 98 Redux, featuring engine-level bug fixes, major performance improvements, restored Battlezone 1.5 behavior, multiplayer/netcode improvements, modern input and rendering options, expanded HUD/PDA systems, and extensively rewritten campaign missions.[/i]

[h2]Important Notice[/h2]
[b]This project is 100% unofficial and is not affiliated with or supported by Rebellion. It's functional and reasonably stable, but still under active development.[/b]

This patch modifies native game behavior and remains highly experimental. Expect bugs, crashes, compatibility problems, or changes not present in the unmodified game.

Game improvements should be open and shared. Other 'community' patches are closed source, with no way to verify the code is safe or to contribute. Here all source code is public on Github, and you can build it yourself.

[h2]Install and Play[/h2]
[b]1. First-time install[/b]
[list=1]
[*] Subscribe and let Steam finish downloading. Do [b]not[/b] enable anything in the Mods menu.
[*] Download and run [url=https://github.com/GrizzlyOne95/Battlezone98Redux_Shim/releases/latest/download/OpenShimSetup.exe]OpenShimSetup.exe[/url]. It installs the complete OpenShim suite.
[*] Start the game. (No installer? In the game, open [b]Single Player > Instant Action[/b] (bottom right) and start [b]! SETUP / REPAIR - Open Community Patch[/b], then [b]exit the game completely[/b] and start it again. The files are put in place while the game is closed.)
[/list]

[b]2. Where the campaign is[/b]
Open [b]Single Player > Custom Campaign[/b] (top right) and choose [b]Campaign Reimagined[/b]. It holds the full 17-mission NSDF campaign, from [b]Red Arrival[/b] to [b]The Ultimate Quake[/b]. The early missions are the most polished; the last few are still in development. Every mission is also in the multiplayer list as [b]CR 01[/b] to [b]CR 17 Coop[/b] for up to four players.
Campaign assets load only with this campaign. OpenShim's engine fixes stay active game-wide, and all other content uses its usual menus.

[b]3. Updating[/b]
Once OpenShim is installed, updates install automatically. After the Workshop item updates, the game stages the new OpenShim when you start a campaign mission or reach the main menu, and installs it when you quit the game. You don't need the installer or the setup mission again. To update by hand, open [b]Options[/b], go to the [b]OpenShim[/b] page and press [b]Check for Updates[/b] (Steam only). Run the installer or Setup / Repair again only if the install is damaged.

[b]Guarded and Reversible:[/b] OpenShim validates the game build and patch sites, fails closed on mismatches, and never modifies battlezone98redux.exe on disk.

If setup fails, check [i]openshim_update.status[/i] and [i]winmm_replace.log[/i]. Manual installs need the [url=https://github.com/GrizzlyOne95/Battlezone98Redux_Shim/releases]complete OpenShim suite[/url]; winmm.dll alone is not enough. Remove other native DLL mods before troubleshooting.

[h2]Major Player-Facing Improvements[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Game-Wide Native Patch:[/b] OpenShim isn't limited to Campaign Reimagined. Engine fixes, input improvements, multiplayer fixes, HUD options, networking changes, crash protection, and many other features work across the stock campaigns, Instant Action, multiplayer, and compatible mods.
[*] [b]Remastered Worlds (DX11 Enhanced):[/b] High-resolution terrain packs for all nine worlds. The stock textures remain the fallback on other renderers.
[*] [b]Destruction Debris:[/b] Restored the classic Battlezone 1.5 behavior where destroyed vehicles and buildings break into visible physical geometry chunks. These aren't estimations - they track exactly with the legacy hidden GEOs. They're the real deal.
[*] [b] Massive FPS and optimization boosts: [/b] Removed major rendering bottlenecks: redundant Ogre geometry rebuilds, excess destruction submissions, broken craft culling and needless DX11 CPU/GPU syncs. Benchmarks show 5-15% gains in representative CPU-heavy scenarios, with improvements exceeding 70% in destruction-heavy stress tests.
[*] [b]Multiplayer:[/b] Fixed the server list jumping to the top on refresh and a crash when creating a game; removed the ~30-second hang on leaving a match by caching compiled shaders; team flags above player vehicles, toggleable live. Massive netcode improvements to help stability in longer matches.
[*] [b]Audio Reliability:[/b] Larger sound-channel pool, so fewer dropouts in big battles and dialogue-heavy missions.
[*] [b]Native AutoSave:[/b] A dedicated AutoSave entry that doesn't consume normal save slots. Works in ALL single player content including Instant Action missions. 
[*] [b]Real Crash Diagnostics:[/b] Native crash logging and minidump capture turn mysterious Redux crashes into actionable module/address reports, making engine-level bugs substantially easier to reproduce and fix.
[/list]

[h2]In-Game Options and Controls[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]OpenShim Options Page:[/b] New settings pages on the stock Options screen; most apply instantly, and hovering a row explains it. Includes Raw Mouse Input (bypassing legacy mouse smoothing/acceleration), custom keybindings, attack alerts, target popups, scrap/pilot HUD style, jet flames, unit voices, weapon and reticle convergence, smarter scavengers, anti-air turret pitch, jump-snipe crouch, global turbo, and player/AI headlights with colour and beam controls.
[*] [b]Renderer Profiles:[/b] Switch between stock-compatible Redux presentation, enhanced rendering, and retro-oriented presentation through OpenShim's native renderer-profile system, with optional DX11-specific visual features.
[*] [b]Rewritten Key Binding Screen:[/b] Rebind controls in-game across both control families, with paging, live key capture, and cancel, written safely back to your key map.
[*] [b]Career tracking:[/b] Added a dedicated main menu button for Career stats, if you have that turned on in OpenShim settings. Kills, deaths, etc. 
[*] [b]Better Multiplayer Hosting:[/b] Native host controls, persistent player bans, improved network tuning, vehicle flags, nickname/network settings, clearer multiplayer failure diagnostics, and fixes for several stock lobby/UI problems.
[/list]

[h2]Restored Legacy Battlezone Behavior[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Classic HUD Layout Option:[/b] Restored legacy-style scrap and pilot meter placement aligned with the command interface and native HUD panels.
[*] [b]Jump-Snipe Crouch:[/b] Restored the classic crouch while sniping mid-jump. Single-player only.
[*] [b]Satellite fog of war:[/b] Redux broke the fog of war, so you can see everything on the map even if its not in radar range. This is now fixed.
[/list]

[h2]Platform Support[/h2]
Windows and Linux (including Steam Deck, through Proton or Wine) are supported on Steam and GOG, running the same files. If something works on one and not another, please report it.

[h2]Uninstallation[/h2]
Delete [b]winmm.dll[/b] from the game folder to return to unpatched startup. The campaign needs the patch; unsubscribe for full removal.

[h2]Reporting Issues[/h2]
Please avoid reports such as 'it does not work.' Detailed reproduction steps make it much more likely a problem gets fixed. Include the mission or mode, what you saw, and a zipped [b]logs[/b] folder.

[h2]AI-Assisted Development:[/h2]
Anthropic's Claude and OpenAI's GPT Sol models are extremely adept at reverse engineering and writing patches, so I use them to save time and help with long tedious tasks. All work is designed, implemented, tested, and reviewed by me.
